   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to the prevention of\nsuicide; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2017, amending the mental\nhygiene law relating to establishing the adolescent suicide prevention\nadvisory council, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 5500-C and A.\n7225-B, in relation to the effectiveness thereof; and repealing section 41.56\nof the mental hygiene law relating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S7322",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7322-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 20,
       "fullName": "Jesse Hamilton",
       "imgName": "889_jesse_hamilton.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 889,
       "sessionMemberId": 937,
       "sessionYear": 2017,
       "shortName": "HAMILTON"
      },
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 32,
       "fullName": "Luis R. Sepúlveda",
       "imgName": "493_Luis_Sepulveda.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1142,
       "sessionMemberId": 1140,
       "sessionYear": 2017,
       "shortName": "SEPULVEDA"
      }
     ],
     "size": 2
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§41.56 & 7.07, Ment Hyg L; amd §2, Chap of 2017 (as proposed in S. 5500-C and A. 7225-B)",
    "lawSection": "Mental Hygiene Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7322\n\nSPONSOR: ALCANTARA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to\nthe prevention of suicide; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2017,\namending the mental hygiene law relating to establishing the adolescent\nsuicide prevention advisory council, as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S. 5500-C and A. 7225-B, in relation to the effectiveness there-\nof; and repealing section 41.56 of the mental hygiene law relating ther-\neto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAdds suicide research, prevention and reduction to the scope of respon-\nsibilities for the Office of Mental Health under the mental hygiene law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 repeals section 41.56 of the mental hygiene law as added by\nchapter 436 of the laws of 2017.\n\nSection 2 amends section 7.07 of the mental hygiene law to add a new\nsubdivision (g) that would add suicide prevention, research and\nreduction to the responsibilities of the Office of Mental Health.\n\nSection 3 amends section 2 of chapter 436 of the laws of 2017 to make\nthe act effective immediately.\n\nSection 4 provides an immediate effective date, provided however, that\nsections 1 and 2 shall take effect on the same date and in the same\nmanner as chapter 436 of the laws of 2017.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nSection 7.07 of the mental hygiene law sets forth the responsibilities\nof the Office of Mental Health.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSince 2004 the suicide rate in the State of New York has been on the\nrise. The Office of Mental Health has been on the front lines in the\nfight to prevent suicide and has been operating a number of programs to\nreduce incidences of suicide. Unfortunately, the Office is not official-\nly tasked with suicide prevention, research and reduction.  This bill\nwould make suicide prevention a responsibility of the Office and given\nthe steady increase in suicide over the last decade, this function is\nessential in protecting all New Yorkers.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNegotiated chapter amendment to chapter 436 of the laws of 2017.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately, provided however, that sections\none and two of this act shall take effect on the same date and in the\nsame manner as chapter 436 of the laws of 2017, amending the mental\nhygiene law relating to establishing the adolescent suicide prevention\nadvisory council, as proposed in legislative bill numbers 5.5500-C and\nA.7225-B, takes effect\n",
